Script 16: Automated Directory Sync & Integrity Verification (sync_verify.sh)

Copies files between two directories and verifies data integrity using MD5 hashes.

    Concepts: rsync / cp, md5sum, for loop matching.

Bash

#!/bin/bash
SRC="./src_dir"
DEST="./dest_dir"

mkdir -p "$SRC" "$DEST"
# Create a test file if empty
echo "Sample Content" > "$SRC/test.txt"

echo "Syncing $SRC to $DEST..."
cp -r "$SRC"/* "$DEST"/

echo "Verifying file integrity..."
for file in "$SRC"/*; do
    filename=$(basename "$file")
    SRC_HASH=$(md5sum "$file" | awk '{print $1}')
    DEST_HASH=$(md5sum "$DEST/$filename" | awk '{print $1}')
    
    if [ "$SRC_HASH" == "$DEST_HASH" ]; then
        echo " [MATCH] $filename ($SRC_HASH)"
    else
        echo " [MISMATCH] $filename integrity check failed!"
    fi
done

Application: Verifies that file backup copies match the source files bit-for-bit without corruption.

